set.seed(2408)
x &lt;- gsea$d$rtm$tu_het
if (between(sum(x$Sig), 1, 50)) {
    gsea_node_network(x, TRUE)
} else {
    pander(glue(
        "**No plot generated because number of significant pathways is ",
        "{ifelse(
            sum(x$Sig) &lt; 1,
            'less than 1.',
            'greater than 50.'
        )}**"
    ))
}





Network analysis of the significantly enriched pathways. Coloured nodes represent pathways, black nodes represent leading edge genes. The relative size of pathway nodes is determined by -log10(p). Pathways that cluster close together share leading edge genes. Pathway nodes are labelled by their respective name, and in the case of directional GSEA, upregulated pathways are colour blue and downregulated pathways are coloured red.






